WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.316 --> 00:00:03.394
- Way bigger businesses than you

00:00:03.394 --> 00:00:07.424
have been put out of business
because of technology shifts.

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:09.694
When I invested in 
Uber five years ago,

00:00:09.694 --> 00:00:13.243
I called my dad's 
Russian friends in L.A.

00:00:13.243 --> 00:00:15.813
They came to this 
country in '78, '79.

00:00:15.813 --> 00:00:17.143
They were dead broke.

00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:18.824
They lived in studio apartments.

00:00:18.824 --> 00:00:22.303
They drove taxi cabs for
two, three bucks an hour.

00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:25.523
Hustled their way, worked every
hour, no Saturday and Sunday

00:00:25.523 --> 00:00:28.362
for 20 years, built up a
business, didn't buy anything,

00:00:28.362 --> 00:00:30.826
saved all their money,
eventually bought their own car,

00:00:30.826 --> 00:00:34.400
eventually had four or five
guys or girls underneath them,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.350
built a business, 
had the American dream,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.371
finally got into 
their 50s and 60s,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.682
worked every goddamn 
minute to get there,

00:00:40.682 --> 00:00:43.851
and now were gonna kind of,
like, enjoy it a little bit.

00:00:43.851 --> 00:00:45.979
And then Uber came along.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.859
And so I called 
Marik and Vladimir

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:50.100
and these guys and said, "Hey."

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.041
Vladimir, I know.

00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:56.248
And said, "Vlad, I've got
good news and bad news.

00:00:56.248 --> 00:00:58.899
"Good news is you've
done well and

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:00.667
"America's the greatest 
country in the world.

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.649
"Bad news is you 
might be in trouble."

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:05.318
And literally, the
three of them, verbatim,

00:01:05.318 --> 00:01:08.818
were all like, "That's nice,
boy chick, we'll be okay.

00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:11.908
"So, what you're telling me
is they're gonna take a phone

00:01:11.908 --> 00:01:14.617
"and hit a button and
the car is gonna come?

00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:17.556
"Very good, very good,
I'll talk to you later."

00:01:17.556 --> 00:01:19.666
That's a funny story 
and I say it funny.

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:21.116
Here's what's not funny:

00:01:21.116 --> 00:01:23.356
every one of those 
three guys' businesses

00:01:23.356 --> 00:01:25.016
have been slaughtered.

00:01:25.016 --> 00:01:26.356
Absolutely slaughtered.

00:01:26.356 --> 00:01:27.566
All of their businesses now,

00:01:27.566 --> 00:01:28.936
that they're trying to sell,

00:01:28.936 --> 00:01:31.965
are literally worth 
15 cents on the dollar

00:01:31.965 --> 00:01:34.205
of what it was worth 
just four years ago.

00:01:34.205 --> 00:01:36.024
(light music)

